WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:08.700
The genome of human cells is arranged
in 46 chromosomes. So, random sorting

2
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:14.450
of the DNA would almost certainly lead
to errors. Indeed, many human diseases

3
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:20.350
are caused by this type of error. To
avoid this problem, cells with nuclei

4
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:24.890
have evolved a precise chromosome
division process called mitosis.

5
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.560
In preparation for mitosis,

6
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.710
the cell first makes a copy of all of
its DNA.

7
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:39.030
During the process of DNA replication,
a protein complex called cohesin is

8
00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:45.330
laid down to hold the two resultant
sister chromatids together. Now the

9
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:46.310
cell enters mitosis.

10
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:54.190
An important structure called the
mitotic spindle forms. This structure

11
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.830
is made up of many long fibers of
protein, called microtubules,

12
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.490
that attach to chromatids.

13
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.280
Once attached, the spindle pulls on the
chromatids, but the sisters won't

14
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:14.050
separate because they are held together
by cohesin. In order for mitosis to

15
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:20.070
proceed, every pair of sister
chromatids must be attached and

16
00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:25.800
pointing towards opposite ends of the
spindle. The cell has a sensing pathway

17
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.950
to wait until this condition is met.

18
00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:34.980
Once the chromosomes are all correctly
attached, a protein that cuts cohesin

19
00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:40.990
is activated. Now that the connection
is cut, microtubules can pull sister

20
00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:47.110
chromatids in opposite directions.
Importantly, this means that each side

21
00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:52.470
of the cell gets exactly one copy of
every chromosome. Now the cell can

22
00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:58.250
divide to create two daughter cells,
each with a precise copy of the genome.

